OL,3,GNEWSAKent's role in first Ordnance
OL,4,ASurvey map marked
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe first Ordnance Survey map, which
OL,7,Fcovered Kent and became a blueprint for
OL,8,Fmodern mapping, is being celebrated 225
OL,9,Fyears after its publication.
OL,11,FPublished in 1801, the map was produced
OL,12,Fover fears of a Napoleonic invasion
OL,13,Falong the south coast.
OL,15,FSurveyors spent more than a decade
OL,16,Fmeasuring the landscape, and tackling
OL,17,Fbogs and marshland while using
OL,18,Fpioneering techniques and detailed
OL,19,Ffield observations to create a
OL,20,Fcomprehensive map of the county.
OL,23,APub: 02-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,323,320,200,140,0,100
